WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.681
Seven complementary projects turn
the program's most common gaps

2
00:00:04.681 --> 00:00:08.975
into executable work, each with
its own sponsor, lead and pilot.

3
00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:13.436
In their suggested starting order:
Identity Lifecycle and Provisioning;

4
00:00:13.436 --> 00:00:17.752
Endpoint and Device Modernization;
Network and Access Modernization;

5
00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:20.677
Continuous Monitoring
and the Evidence Fabric;

6
00:00:20.677 --> 00:00:25.139
Privileged Access and Administrative
Identity; Data Platform Identity

7
00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:29.088
Transformation; and Supply Chain
and Software Bill of Materials.

8
00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:31.501
The order says which project has to be far

9
00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:34.199
enough along before the
next can show results.

10
00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:39.419
Identity is first, because everything
else consumes its attributes and owners;

11
00:00:39.419 --> 00:00:44.400
a device project started on unreliable
attributes produces policy bypass.

12
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.643
Monitoring comes fourth,
because an evidence fabric

13
00:00:47.643 --> 00:00:50.887
needs at least two sources
already emitting records.

14
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:54.950
Privileged access is chartered fifth,
but it isn't fifth in practice:

15
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:59.881
the Foundation gate already needs emergency
access accounts vaulted and tested,

16
00:00:59.881 --> 00:01:04.088
and Tier 0 administrators registered
for phishing-resistant sign-in.

17
00:01:04.088 --> 00:01:07.938
Every charter asks for a working
pilot, not a finished estate.

18
00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:10.388
Two rules keep the portfolio coherent.

19
00:01:10.388 --> 00:01:13.157
No project designates
a second authoritative

20
00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:15.713
source for something another project owns.

21
00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:20.726
And every project emits evidence in the
shape the monitoring project defines.

22
00:01:20.726 --> 00:01:23.951
The projects don't form a
second governance structure,

23
00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:26.675
and no project clears a
program gate on its own.

24
00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:29.821
Filling in their names is
each project's first act,

25
00:01:29.821 --> 00:01:32.810
and every project lead
reports to the steward.
